2Co 1:1 , Paul salutes the Corinthians;
2Co 1:3 , he encourages them against troubles, by the comforts and deliverances which God had given him, as in all his afflictions
2Co 1:8 , so particularly in his late danger in Asia;
2Co 1:12 , And calling both his own conscience and theirs to witness of his sincere manner of preaching the immutable truth of the gospel
2Co 1:15 . he excuses his not coming to them, as proceeding not of lightness, but of his lenity towards them.
